# The three cloudflare spend-belt alerts (#217) that carry a `for:` window over a single-replica
# scrape — the class #288/#313/#328 hardened elsewhere and homelab#334 ports here — lifted
# VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped, the manifest is their one home).
# This is the rules file that spend-belt.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to
# anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a
# PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named
# .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under
# argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would fail it.
#
# The FIRST fixture pair in this directory (FU-158's behaviour half, #334). It covers 3 of the
# CR's 5 alerts; CloudflareExporterDown and CloudflareEdge5xx have no behaviour test yet — honest
# remaining work, listed in #334's PR body.
#
# ⚠ NOT DRIFT-PINNED (the general harness that would extract `.spec.groups` at run time lives in
# `scripts/**` + `.github/**`, outside the fixer lane's tier — homelab#337). A stale hand copy
# tests the OLD expr and passes VACUOUSLY. Re-copy after every expr edit:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "cloudflare-spend-belt", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabled" or .alert == "CloudflareZonePlanNotFree" or .alert == "CloudflareSpendProbeBlind")]}]}' argocd/resources/cloudflare-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#
# …that command regenerates the `cloudflare-spend-belt` group ONLY. The `regression-witness-pre-334`
# group at the bottom is not in the CR and must survive the re-copy — re-append it (see its header).
# (One line on purpose: `devbox run` executes scripts under dash, which mangles a multi-line
# quoted argument — CLAUDE.md §Environment.)
#
# The OTHER check over these same exprs is `devbox run spend-probe-self-test`, which reads them out
# of the committed CR and replays them against fixtures built by the real collector. It evaluates
# ONE instant, so it cannot see a `for:` window or a scrape hole — it pins the metric names, the
# polarity, the thresholds, the zone selection and (since #334) the bridge's direction and range.
# Behaviour over time is this file's job. Neither subsumes the other.
groups:
  - name: cloudflare-spend-belt
    rules:
      - alert: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabled
        expr: max by (zone) (max_over_time(cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing[10m])) > 0
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
        annotations:
          summary: Usage-billed toggle enabled on Cloudflare zone {{ $labels.zone }}
          description: 'Argo Smart Routing is no longer "off" on zone {{ $labels.zone }} — a per-GB usage-billed feature, which bills the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: Cloudflare audit log for who/when (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix lists which tokens carry Zone Settings Write), then GET /zones/{id}/argo/smart_routing to confirm the live value.'
      - alert: CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
        expr: min by (zone) (min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free[10m])) == 0
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
        annotations:
          summary: Cloudflare product zone {{ $labels.zone }} is no longer on the free plan
          description: 'Zone {{ $labels.zone }} reports a plan other than free — a recurring charge on the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY (a deliberate upgrade looks identical to an accidental one). Check: Cloudflare audit log, and whether the change was intended; the two watched zones are the product zones only, eid-demo.com is out of scope by design.'
      - alert: CloudflareSpendProbeBlind
        expr: min by (zone) (min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok[10m])) == 0 or absent(min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok[10m]))
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
        annotations:
          summary: Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind{{ if $labels.zone }} on zone {{ $labels.zone }}{{ end }}
          description: 'The spend-toggle probe has not read a zone''s plan/Argo state for 30m — the gauges above are UNKNOWN, not safe, and a toggle flipped now would go unnoticed. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: pod + logs (deploy/cloudflare-spend-probe in monitoring, it logs every failed read), the cloudflare-exporter-token Secret (ESO ← Infisical CLOUDFLARE_OBSERVABILITY_READ), then the token''s Zone Settings Read on both product zones (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix).'

  # ── REGRESSION WITNESS — NOT deployed rules, and deliberately not in prometheusrule.yaml ──────
  # The three pre-#334 exprs, verbatim, plus one alert that never shipped at all. Each is checked
  # at the SAME eval times as its shipped twin in spend-belt.promtool-test, so every claim the
  # manifest makes about the class ("the roll restarted this window", "the absent() arm swapped the
  # alert's identity") is executed against the form that had the defect rather than asserted about
  # it. `for:`, thresholds and `severity` are carried unchanged — only the expr differs, which is
  # what keeps the contrast attributable to the bridge alone. Annotations are trimmed to `summary`,
  # the convention the openrouter-proxy and github-exporter witness groups already use: the fixture
  # asserts WHEN each witness fires, and the description templates are pinned on the shipped side.
  # Fossils, not copies: if any of the three exprs is revisited, this group stays as it is. It is
  # also what stops a STALE hand copy of the group above from passing vacuously — with the old expr
  # in both places the pairs would agree and every roll assertion below fails.
  - name: regression-witness-pre-334
    rules:
      - alert: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabledPre334
        expr: cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing > 0
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Usage-billed toggle enabled on Cloudflare zone {{ $labels.zone }}
      - alert: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreePre334
        expr: cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free == 0
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Cloudflare product zone {{ $labels.zone }} is no longer on the free plan
      - alert: CloudflareSpendProbeBlindPre334
        expr: cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok == 0 or absent(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok)
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind{{ if $labels.zone }} on zone {{ $labels.zone }}{{ end }}
      # NOT a pre-fix form and NOT a proposal: the MECHANICAL PORT, i.e. what CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
      # would be if #328's idiom had been copied without asking which direction preserves the alert.
      # `plan_is_free == 0` is LOW-is-bad, so `max_over_time` reads the healthiest sample of the last
      # 10m and delays a genuine plan upgrade by the whole range. The fixture's direction case shows
      # it paging 10 minutes after the shipped alert — two of its `for: 5m` windows — on a belt whose
      # entire job is to notice a charge starting. Kept here so that claim is executed.
      # CloudflareSpendProbeBlind shares the direction and the argument; it is asserted once.
      - alert: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreeMaxDirection
        expr: max by (zone) (max_over_time(cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free[10m])) == 0
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Cloudflare product zone {{ $labels.zone }} is no longer on the free plan
